{:lib      io.github.buddhilw/monero-store
 :minor    6
 :license  {:name "MIT" :url "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"}
 :scm-url  "https://github.com/BuddhiLW/monero-store-template"

 ;; The money path, plus the two adapters an EMBEDDING store CALLS rather than
 ;; deploys: the kontor ledger, and the monero-wallet-rpc chain wallet. jdbc and
 ;; stripe stay unpublished on their own source roots — those are for deploying
 ;; THIS store, and a host that embeds the money path already has a database and
 ;; has already chosen a card processor.
 ;;
 ;; monero-rpc ships because operating Monero is the one thing an embedding
 ;; store cannot supply for itself. Without it a consumer resolving the
 ;; coordinate gets `IChainWallet` and no implementation that talks to a wallet,
 ;; so it writes a second one — which is exactly how two copies of one adapter
 ;; come to exist and then drift apart.
 ;;
 ;; This still ships zero vendor jars. kontor and monero-java are alias deps,
 ;; never transitive ones, so each namespace loads only for a consumer that put
 ;; that SDK on its own classpath — and a consumer that keeps no book, or that
 ;; watches through a gateway instead of running a wallet, never requires it.
 :src-dirs ["src" "resources" "adapters/kontor/src" "adapters/monero-rpc/src"]

 :publish  :clojars}
